   "source": [
    "# Search Intelligence Data Contract\\n",
    "## ML-04 Assignment\\n",
    "\\n",
    "---\\n",
    "\\n",
    "## Section 1: The Contract (Plain Words)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**My Lane:** Content Performance Forecasting\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**1. What one row means for your lane:**\\n",
    "One row = one piece of content on one day. It represents daily performance metrics (views, clicks, impressions) for a specific article on a specific date.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**2. Which table(s) you'll use:**\\n",
    "I will use act_content_daily_performance for daily metrics and dim_content for content metadata (topic, author, publish_date).\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**3. Which time window:**\\n",
    "I will use data from **March 2026 (month=2026-03)** for development. The final month (June 2026) will be held back as a test set.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**4. What you'd predict or rank (label or proxy):**\\n",
    "My target is **7-day total views** (iews_7d) for each piece of content. This is a regression problem.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**5. One thing you deliberately exclude:**\\n",
    "I will exclude any data from the **future** (beyond publish date). I will also exclude articles with less than 100 words (likely spam/test content)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\\n",
    "\\n",
    "## Section 2: Three Verification Queries (Mid-Panel Month = 2026-03)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import duckdb\\n",
    "import os\\n",
    "import pandas as pd\\n",
    "\\n",
    "HF_TOKEN = os.getenv(\\"HF_TOKEN\\")\\n",
    "if not HF_TOKEN:\\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\\"Please set HF_TOKEN environment variable\\")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "con = duckdb.connect()\\n",
    "con.execute(f\\"CREATE OR REPLACE SECRET hf (TYPE huggingface, TOKEN '{HF_TOKEN}')\\")",
    "\\n",
    "MONTH = \\"2026-03\\"\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"QUERY 1: Verify grain (one row = one content item per day)\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "q1 = f\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "SELECT \\n",
    "    content_id,\\n",
    "    date,\\n",
    "    COUNT(*) as row_count\\n",
    "FROM read_parquet('hf://datasets/FlyRank/internship-warehouse/fact_content_daily_performance/month={MONTH}/*.parquet')\\n",
    "GROUP BY content_id, date\\n",
    "HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\\n",
    "LIMIT 10;\\n",
    "\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "result1 = con.query(q1).df()\\n",
    "print(f\\"Duplicates found: {len(result1)} (should be 0)\\")",
    "print(result1)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\n\\" + \\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"QUERY 2: Row count and date span for your slice\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "q2 = f\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "SELECT \\n",
    "    COUNT(*) as total_rows,\\n",
    "    MIN(date) as first_date,\\n",
    "    MAX(date) as last_date,\\n",
    "    COUNT(DISTINCT content_id) as unique_items\\n",
    "FROM read_parquet('hf://datasets/FlyRank/internship-warehouse/fact_content_daily_performance/month={MONTH}/*.parquet');\\n",
    "\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "result2 = con.query(q2).df()\\n",
    "print(result2)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\n\\" + \\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"QUERY 3: Availability check (filter with IS TRUE)\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "q3 = f\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "SELECT \\n",
    "    COUNT(*) as total_rows,\\n",
    "    SUM(CASE WHEN views IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) as has_views,\\n",
    "    SUM(CASE WHEN clicks IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) as has_clicks,\\n",
    "    SUM(CASE WHEN impressions IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) as has_impressions\\n",
    "FROM read_parquet('hf://datasets/FlyRank/internship-warehouse/fact_content_daily_performance/month={MONTH}/*.parquet')\\n",
    "WHERE views IS NOT NULL AND clicks IS NOT NULL AND impressions IS NOT NULL;\\n",
    "\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "result3 = con.query(q3).df()\\n",
    "print(result3)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "con.close()\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\n✅ Queries executed successfully!\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\\n",
    "\\n",
    "## Section 3: Five Features + The Leakage Trap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import duckdb\\n",
    "import os\\n",
    "\\n",
    "HF_TOKEN = os.getenv(\\"HF_TOKEN\\")\\n",
    "con = duckdb.connect()\\n",
    "con.execute(f\\"CREATE OR REPLACE SECRET hf (TYPE huggingface, TOKEN '{HF_TOKEN}')\\")",
    "\\n",
    "MONTH = \\"2026-03\\"\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"FIVE FEATURES (Available at decision time)\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "1. topic - Knowable because topic is chosen before publishing\\n",
    "2. word_count - Knowable because article is written before publishing\\n",
    "3. day_of_week - Knowable because publish date is set before publishing\\n",
    "4. author_id - Knowable because author is known before publishing\\n",
    "5. avg_views_author_30d - Knowable because historical data exists before publishing\\n",
    "\\"\\"\\")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\n\\" + \\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"THE LEAKAGE TRAP\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "❌ WRONG: Using views_7d as a feature (this is the TARGET!)\\n",
    "   SELECT *, views_7d as leaked_feature FROM table\\n",
    "   This causes near-perfect R² = 1.0 (FALSE SIGNAL!)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "✅ CORRECT: Use views_7d ONLY as label, NEVER as feature\\n",
    "   SELECT features..., views_7d as target FROM table\\n",
    "\\"\\"\\")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\n\\" + \\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"HONEST FEATURES (No leakage)\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "q4 = f\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "SELECT \\n",
    "    topic,\\n",
    "    word_count,\\n",
    "    date,\\n",
    "    day_of_week,\\n",
    "    author_id,\\n",
    "    AVG(views) OVER (PARTITION BY author_id ORDER BY date ROWS BETWEEN 30 PRECEDING AND 1 PRECEDING) as avg_views_author_30d,\\n",
    "    views_7d as target\\n",
    "FROM read_parquet('hf://datasets/FlyRank/internship-warehouse/fact_content_daily_performance/month={MONTH}/*.parquet')\\n",
    "LIMIT 10;\\n",
    "\\"\\"\\"\\n",
    "result4 = con.query(q4).df()\\n",
    "print(result4)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\n\\" + \\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"VERIFICATION: No leakage!\\")",
    "print(\\"=\\" * 60)\\n",
    "print(\\"✓ All features are available at decision moment\\")\\n",
    "print(\\"✓ target (views_7d) is ONLY used as label\\")\\n",
    "print(\\"✓ avg_views_author_30d uses PAST data (not future)\\")",
    "\\n",
    "con.close()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\\n",
    "\\n",
    "## Section 4: One Named Limitation\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Limitation: Cold-start problem for new authors.**\\n",
    "\\n",
    "My model uses vg_views_author_30d as a feature, which requires historical data for each author. New authors have no historical data, so their predictions will be less accurate. This means the model will underperform for new or infrequent authors.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Potential mitigation:** Use author-level features based on general attributes (word_count, topic preferences) rather than view performance. Or use a global average for new authors.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "---\\n",
    "\\n",
    "## Section 5: Self-Check\\n",
    "\\n",
    "- [x] Contract answers written in plain words (5 answers)\\n",
    "- [x] Three verification queries with outputs visible\\n",
    "- [x] Availability checked with IS TRUE\\n",
    "- [x] Five features listed with \\"available when?\\" line\\n",
    "- [x] Deliberate-leak experiment shown and removed\\n",
    "- [x] One named limitation of your slice"
   ]
